course: dictionary
lesson: 9370
title: One word, many uses: spoon
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A spoon is a small tool with a round, shallow end and a handle. You use it to eat, to serve food, or to stir. «When a table is laid, every person gets a knife, a fork and a spoon.» Here spoon is a thing on the table.
explain: Spoon can also be a measure. «Add a spoon of sugar» means the amount a spoon holds, which is a spoonful. In cooking, teaspoons and tablespoons are measures, so the word tells you how much to use.
explain: Spoon can be a verb too. To spoon food means to move it with a spoon. Check the sentence: if the word could be swapped for «move with a spoon» and still make sense, spoon is doing a job, not naming a thing.
explain: Look at the words around spoon. «Never put hands or a spoon into a blender while it is running.» The words never and running warn you that it is not safe. The context tells you what to do, not just what the word means.
fact: A spoon is a tool with a round, shallow end and a handle.
fact: A spoonful is the amount a spoon holds, as in a spoon of sugar.
fact: To spoon food means to move it with a spoon.
fact: Metal carries heat, so a metal spoon in hot soup gets hot.
fact: «A girl in Sydney reaches into the washing-up for a spoon and finds a sharp knife instead.» Context shows that a spoon is a thing you can pick up from a sink full of washing-up.
exercise: «When a table is laid, every person gets a knife, a fork and a spoon.» How many pieces of cutlery does each person get? | 4 | 1 | 2 | *3
exercise: Mum says, «Add one spoon of sugar.» What does spoon mean here? | A kind of table | A fruit | To stir the tea | *The amount a spoon holds
exercise: «Never put hands or a spoon into a blender while it is running.» What is the lesson in this sentence? | Blenders are safe to use with spoons | Spoons make a blender run faster | *Keep spoons and hands away from a running blender | A blender needs a spoon to start
test: «Please spoon the soup into the bowls.» What does spoon mean here? | A fruit | A kind of table | *To move soup with a spoon | A metal drawer
test: Why does a metal spoon get hot when it is left in hot soup? | *Because metal carries heat | Because soup is cold | Because spoons are always hot | Because spoons like warm things
exam: In «She added a spoon of salt», what does spoon mean? | To stir with | A tool for eating | A fruit | *The amount a spoon holds
